# Deny-all allowlist. This repo is published publicly, and the project folder
# holds client freight data, reports and results that must never be pushed.
# Everything is ignored by default; only the files the app needs are re-added.
#
# A new source file will NOT be tracked until a "!" line is added for it.
/*

!.gitignore
!.gitattributes
!README.md
!Dockerfile
!requirements.txt
!app.py
!config.py
!projects.yaml
!cache.db
!core/
!agents/
!ui/
!tests/
!tools/
!.streamlit/

# ...but never the compiled artefacts inside those packages
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Runtime scratch dirs created by config.py. The station gazetteer lives under
# data/ but is a bundled asset rather than scratch, so it is re-added.
#
# Note the "data/*" rather than "data/". Git will not re-include a file whose
# parent directory is excluded, so "data/" followed by "!data/stations.csv"
# silently keeps the gazetteer out of the repo. Excluding the directory's
# *contents* leaves the directory itself readable, and the negation works.
!data/
data/*
!data/stations.csv
output/
